# Bench-only fragment. NEVER part of a release.
#
# It adds TWO exceptions to the product profile, and they are two symbols rather
# than one because the record of which safety evidence a build went without is
# the entire point of having them:
#
#   HK_BENCH_AUDIO_WITHOUT_PROFILE          No G0/G2 driver-protection profile
#                                           exists, so there is no crossover, no
#                                           protective high-pass and no limiter
#                                           ceiling in front of the amplifier.
#
#   HK_BENCH_AUDIO_WITHOUT_POWER_TELEMETRY  No ADC driver (F6) and no G3/G4
#                                           thresholds exist, so the pack cannot
#                                           be judged at all -- and neither can
#                                           ADR-0004's "not while charging".
#
# TOGETHER THEY RELEASE THE AMPLIFIER, and that is a change from what this file
# used to mean. Until 2026-09-08 nothing in this firmware ever drove
# HK_PIN_AMP_MUTE or HK_PIN_DAC_XSMT, so the exception above bought a clocked
# I2S bus and nothing else. hk_audio_hw now drives both lines, and it releases
# them when both gates say yes. With both symbols set, a DAC on the I2S pins and
# an amplifier on the mute line, full-scale AirPlay audio reaches whatever is
# wired to that amplifier's output, with nothing in front of it.
#
# So the standard for "defensible" has moved with it. This is defensible into a
# dummy load, into a scope, or into nothing at all. It is NOT defensible into
# the Nova drivers: their individual impedance is still the open G0 blocker, and
# without it there is no informed limit on what the amplifier may be asked to
# produce. Look at what is connected to the speaker terminals before you flash
# a build made from this file.
#
# Build with it:
#   idf.py -C firmware -B firmware/build-bench \
#     -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.bench" \
#     -D SDKCONFIG="$PWD/firmware/build-bench/sdkconfig" build
CONFIG_HK_BENCH_AUDIO_WITHOUT_PROFILE=y
CONFIG_HK_BENCH_AUDIO_WITHOUT_POWER_TELEMETRY=y
# The panel is compiled OUT for now, at the owner's request, while the audio
# path is brought up. Not a blank screen: no SPI bus, no transfers, no pins
# driven. It is the single largest source of periodic switching on this board
# and removing it entirely is the cleanest way to stop it being a variable.
CONFIG_HK_DISPLAY=n
